1
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:22,155
大家请进并找座位坐下，我今天大概只讲半小时到 35 分钟，然后我们要填 CUE 课程评估表。
If people want to make their way in, I'm going to give about a half an hour to a 35 minute lecture today, and then we're going to do the CUE guide forms.

2
00:00:22,155 --> 00:00:52,834
那么，上次我们证明了，如果我们有一个环 R（这是一个整环），我们有如下的蕴涵关系：R 是欧几里得整环，这意味着我们有一个尺度函数（大小函数）从 R - {0} 到正整数集，
So, last time we showed if we had a ring R that we had the following implications (this is a domain): that R is Euclidean, which meant we had a size function from R - {0} to the positive integers, so that you could do a division, you could always do

3
00:00:52,834 --> 00:01:20,417
从而你可以进行带余除法，你总能用 a 去除 b，使得 δ(r) < δ(a)，从而我们在该环中拥有欧几里得辗转相除法；这蕴涵了 R 中的每个理想 I 都是主理想，
a division of b by a so that delta(r) was less than delta(a), so that we had a Euclidean algorithm in the in the ring; that that implied that every ideal I in R is principal, and in fact was generated by an element in it of minimal delta;

4
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:58,999
并且事实上由其中具有最小 δ 值的元素生成；而这又蕴涵了 R 中的每个元素都具有唯一的素元分解：即 R 中的元素 a 可以写成一个单位乘上 R 中若干元素的乘积，
and that that implied that every element in R had a unique prime factorization: namely an element in R, a, could be written as a unit times a product of elements in R where these are prime elements, primes in R,

5
00:01:58,999 --> 00:02:11,444
其中这些都是 R 中的素元，前面是一个单位，且这种分解在相差单位乘子的意义下是唯一的，从而元素 a 决定了这些素因子。
this was a unit, and that this factorization was unique up to multiplication of these primes by units, so that the, um, the element a determined these prime factors.

6
00:02:11,444 --> 00:02:37,280
请记住元素的素性定义：R 中的元素 p 是素元，当且仅当由 p 生成的主理想(p) 是一个非单位理想（即非平凡理想，不等于 R），但在所有主理想中是极大主理想，
So remember that an element is prime, p in R is prime if and only if the principal ideal generated by p is a non-unit ideal, so it's a non-trivial ideal, it's not equal to R, but is maximal with respect to principal ideals,

7
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:49,480
即它不存在因式分解 p = ab 使得 a 或 b 生成比 (p) 更大的主理想；它们要么生成与 (p) 相同的理想，要么生成单位理想（整个环）。
namely there's no factorization of it, p = ab, where either a or b generate a larger ideal than (p); either they generate the same ideal (p), or they generate the unit ideal.

8
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:52,759
因此在主理想的意义下是极大的。
So, maximal with respect to principal ideals.

9
00:02:52,759 --> 00:03:02,830
于是任何元素都有唯一的素元分解，就像在整数中一样。我们证明了若干个环都是欧几里得整环，因而具备所有这些性质。
So that any element has a unique factorization into primes just like in the integers. And we proved that a number of rings were Euclidean, and consequently had all these properties.

10
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:10,628
欧几里得整环的例子：当然包括整数环，这是理论的起点；我们证明了域上的多项式环也是欧几里得整环，
So the examples of Euclidean rings: of course the integers, that's where it started; we showed that polynomials over a field were Euclidean,

11
00:03:10,628 --> 00:03:23,560
其尺度函数就是多项式的次数，最后我们证明了高斯整数环也是欧几里得整环，因此其每个理想都是主理想，且具有唯一分解。
where this function was the degree of the polynomial, and then we showed at the end that the Gaussian integers were Euclidean, so every ideal is principal and we have this factorization.

12
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:29,280
下节课我们将更深入地研究高斯整数环中的素元究竟是什么。
Next time we're going to look more closely at what are the primes in the Gaussian integers.

13
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:37,680
有了这个定理，只有当你真正清楚这些素元长什么样时它才有价值：在整数环中它们是普通的素数，
When you have this theorem, it's only valuable if you really know what the primes look like: so in this ring they're the usual prime numbers,

14
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:50,400
在多项式环中它们是我们所说的不可约多项式；这里是素数，那里是不可约多项式，而下次我们要搞清楚高斯整数环中的素元是什么样。
in this ring they're what we call irreducible polynomials; here it's prime, here it's an irreducible polynomial, and next time we're going to find out what the primes look like in the Gaussian integers.

15
00:03:50,400 --> 00:04:07,439
我们讲了这些蕴涵关系，然后在上节课结束时，我举了一个不具备这两条性质的环的例子，即首先它的理想并不都是主理想，这蕴涵了 R 不是欧几里得整环。
But we did these implications, and then at the end of the lecture I gave an example of a ring which did not have these two properties, namely first of all the ideals were not necessarily principal, and that implied that R wasn't Euclidean.

16
00:04:07,439 --> 00:04:36,000
关于这个环的例子——顺便说一下，另一种表述方式是商环 R/(p) 是一个整环，因为这意味着如果这里的乘积为零，即 a-bar · b-bar ≡ 0 (mod p)，
And the example of a ring—so this, another way of stating this by the way, is that R modulo (p) is an integral domain, because that would say if you had a product in here that was zero, something like a-bar times b-bar is equivalent to 0 mod p,

17
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:49,559
那就意味着 p 必须整除 a 或者 p 必须整除 b，也就是说它不存在非平凡分解，这意味着要么 a-bar = 0，要么 b-bar = 0。
that would mean that either p had to divide a or p had to divide b, namely there were no non-trivial factorizations of it, which would mean that either a-bar was zero or b-bar was zero.

18
00:04:49,559 --> 00:04:56,279
因此素元就是模去其主理想后得到一个整环的元素。
So a prime element is one such that when you mod out by the principal ideal you get an integral domain.

19
00:04:56,279 --> 00:05:06,670
上节课我们证明存在非主理想的方法是：如果这个商环不是域，那么就存在非主理想。
Now the way we showed that there were ideals that were not principal was: if this ring is not a field, then there are non-principal ideals.

20
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:25,840
我们来作一个观察：如果 R/(p) 不是一个域，那么必然存在一个介于 (p) 与 R 之间的理想 I。
So let's make an observation: if R mod (p) is not a field, then there exists an ideal I which is lying between (p) and R.

21
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:36,147
所以如果你能找到一个素元使得这是一个整环但不是域，那就意味着这个商环拥有超过两个理想，对吧？
So if you can find a prime element so that this is a domain but is not a field, that means that this quotient ring has more than two ideals, right?

22
00:05:36,147 --> 00:05:41,360
我们证明过域就是仅有两个理想（零理想与全环）的环。
We proved a field was one where it had only two ideals: zero and the whole ring.

23
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:50,279
如果存在——还记得同构定理：这个商环中的理想，严格对应于 R 中包含 (p) 的理想。
If there are—remember about the isomorphism theorem: the ideals of this ring are exactly the ideals of R that contain (p).

24
00:05:50,279 --> 00:06:01,759
所以如果它不是一个域，就必然存在一个介于 (p) 与 R 之间的非平凡理想，它在该商环中诱导出一个非平凡理想。现在，
So there has to be a non-trivial ideal that lies between (p) and R that creates a non-trivial ideal in this quotient ring if it's not a field. Now that ideal can't be principal,

25
00:06:01,759 --> 00:06:13,360
那个理想不可能是主理想，因为根据素元的定义，(p) 在主理想中是极大的：没有任何包含它的真正的真主理想，因为那会导致因式分解。
because by the definition of being prime, this thing is maximal with respect to principal ideals: nothing contains it that's an actual principal ideal, because that would give a factorization.

26
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:26,760
所以如果你能找到这样一个模主理想的商环是整环但不是域，那么该环就不可能具有“每个理想都是主理想”的性质。
So if you're in the situation where you're able to identify one of these quotients by a principal ideal which is a domain but not a field, then you cannot have this property that every ideal is principal.

27
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:40,760
好，我们给出了一个例子：环取整系数多项式环 Z[x]，素元取 x。
Okay, and we gave an example of this: an example where the ring was polynomials over the integers, and where the prime was x.

28
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:53,120
然后 R/(x) 我们证明了同构于整数环 Z，它是一个整环但不是域。
And then R modulo the ideal generated by x we showed was isomorphic to Z, and that's a domain but not a field.

29
00:06:53,120 --> 00:07:01,615
我还给出了一个包含 (p)的理想 I 的例子：取由 x 和一个素数（如 2）生成的理想 (2, x)。
And I gave an example of an ideal I that contained (p): namely you take the ideal generated by x and a prime number like 2.

30
00:07:01,615 --> 00:07:16,465
它包含理想 (p)，但不等于 R，因为它是把任意整系数多项式在 0 处取值再模 2 的同态的核。
That contains the ideal (p), but it's not equal to R because it's the kernel of the homomorphism that takes an arbitrary integral polynomial, takes its value at 0 mod 2.

31
00:07:16,465 --> 00:07:35,240
这就是映射 R -> Z/2Z，把 f(x)映为 f(0) mod 2，即映为其常数项模 2 的约化。并且存在多项式，例如 f(x)= 1，就不在这个理想中。
So this is the map R -> Z/2Z that takes f(x) to f(0) mod 2, namely it takes it to the mod 2 reduction of its constant term. And there are polynomials like f(x) equal 1, that is not in this ideal.

32
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:48,960
好，所以我们在此给出了一个环的例子，它显然不是主理想环，因为它有一个非平凡且非主的理想，从而不可能拥有欧几里得辗转相除法。
Okay, so we gave an example of a ring here which was certainly not a principal ideal ring, because it had a non-trivial ideal which wasn't principal, and consequently could not have a Euclidean algorithm.

33
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:57,800
但在上节课末尾我告诉过你们，事实上它仍然具有唯一因子分解性质，这是一个比前两者都弱的条件。
But at the end of the lecture I told you that in fact it does still have unique factorization, that this is a weaker condition than either of these two.

34
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:10,603
所以我今天想向大家证明这个结论，因为这是高斯的一个极其出色的成果，而且它正是我们用来在有理数域上对多项式进行因式分解的工具。
So I want to show that to you today, because that's a really great result of Gauss's, and it's what we use to factor polynomials even over the rationals.

35
00:08:10,603 --> 00:08:44,480
这就是我今天要展示给你们的内容：事实上，尽管Z[x] 不是主理想整环，它却具有唯一因子分解性，我们将讲清楚素元是什么等等。
So that's what I'm going to show you today: in fact, even though Z[x] is not a principal ideal domain, it has unique factorization, and we'll say what the primes are and everything.

36
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:56,230
书中还有一个更一般的定理，我今天不打算详细证明，但它是通过这种方法可以得到的结论，通常表述如下：事实上，
And the more general theorem which you can find in the book, which I'm not going to show to you, which is the thing you can get out of this method,

37
00:08:56,230 --> 00:09:24,793
若 R 是一个具有唯一素元分解的整环（UFD），即唯一分解整环，则 R 上的多项式环 R[x] 也是唯一分解整环。
is usually stated the following way: in fact, if R is a domain with unique factorization into primes, so is the ring of polynomials over R, R[x].

38
00:09:24,793 --> 00:09:33,079
你们看，整数环 Z 具有唯一分解，所以我们将看到 Z 上的多项式环 Z[x] 也具有唯一分解。
You see, Z has unique factorization, so we're going to see the polynomials over Z also have unique factorization.

39
00:09:33,079 --> 00:09:51,680
特别地，如果你知道这个推广定理，它不仅意味着一元多项式，还意味着 Z 上的二元多项式环也具有唯一分解，因为一旦我们证明了它有唯一分解，若我们取该环上的多项式，就得到了二元多项式；
So in particular, if you know this extra theorem, that implies not just polynomials in one variable, but polynomials in two variables over Z have unique factorization, because once we prove that this has unique factorization, if we take polynomials over this ring, then we get polynomials in two variables;

40
00:09:51,680 --> 00:10:12,640
或者域上的 n 元多项式环F[x₁, x₂, ..., xₙ] 具有唯一分解，因为域上的一元多项式环具有唯一分解，然后你在此基础上添加另一个变量的多项式环同样具有唯一分解，以此类推。
or polynomials in n variables over a field, F[x_1, x_2, ..., x_n], has unique factorization, because polynomials in one variable over a field have unique factorization, and then you take polynomials over that and another variable, that has unique factorization, and by induction.

41
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:32,440
所以这提供了一种用归纳法证明具有唯一分解的方法，而我们却没有归纳的方法来证明环能保持主理想性质：当你添加一个变量时，绝对不再满足“每个理想都是主理想”。
Okay, so it gives an inductive way of proving that things have unique factorization, whereas we don't have an inductive way of proving that things preserve principal ideals: certainly not the case that if you adjoin a variable you still have every ideal principal.

42
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:42,440
好，现在我们来讨论整系数多项式的因式分解，因为这是今天的主题。刚才那些都算是这堂课的背景。
Okay, so now let's talk about factorization and integral polynomials, because that's the subject today. This was all sort of background to the lecture.

43
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:57,079
大家看，如果我们从一个整系数多项式出发，这是有理系数多项式环的一个子环，而有理数域是一个域。
Now you see, if we start off with a polynomial with integer coefficients, this is a subring of the polynomials with rational coefficients, and the rational numbers are a field.

44
00:10:57,079 --> 00:11:03,639
所以如果我们暂时忘掉自己身处子环中，而只把它看作 Q[x] 中的元素，我们当然可以将其分解为不可约多项式。
So if we forget that we're in this subring and we just look at the element here, we can certainly factor it into irreducible polynomials.

45
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:17,240
我们这样来做：把它写成一个单位乘上 p₁(x) ... p_k(x)，即在 Q[x] 中的因式分解。
So we do that: we write it as a unit times p_1(x) ... p_k(x), a factorization in Q[x].

46
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:26,364
这些多项式是 Q[x] 中的首一不可约多项式。
So these polynomials are monic irreducible polynomials in Q[x].

47
00:11:26,364 --> 00:11:37,040
这完全没有问题，我们只是置身于这个更大的、具有唯一分解的环中，并且这里的单位是一个非零有理数。
There's no problem with that, we just think of ourselves in this larger ring that has unique factorization, and this is a unit which is a non-zero rational number.

48
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:50,880
这种分解是完全唯一的，因为这个环是主理想整环，也是欧几里得整环，所以它具有唯一因子分解。
And that factorization is completely unique, because this is a PID: so this ring is a principal ideal domain, it's a Euclidean domain, so it has unique factorization.

49
00:11:52,120 --> 00:12:15,760
问题在于，首先，这个有理数如果不是整数，可能不在原环中；其次，完全没有理由认为分解中的这些首一多项式会具有整系数。例如，若我取一个简单的多项式 2x + 1，它本身是个极好的整系数多项式，对吧？
The problem is that, first of all, this rational number might not be in this ring if it's not an integer; and secondly, there's no reason that these monic polynomials in the factorization have integral coefficients. So for example, if I took a stupid polynomial like 2x + 1, which is a perfectly nice polynomial with integer coefficients, right?

50
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:37,480
如果我想把它写成这种唯一的分解形式，我会写成 1/2 ... x + 2 ...哎呀抱歉，重来一次。2，写成 2 · (x + 1/2)。很好，因为这里我必须有一个首一多项式。
And I wanted to write it in this unique factored form, I would write it as—one half... x plus two... Oops, sorry, sorry, let's try that again. Two, there we go: 2 * (x + 1/2). Excellent, because here I have to have a monic polynomial.

51
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:46,360
它是一次的所以不可约，这里的 2 就是我的常数 c。这看起来不错，但这根本不行：x + 1/2 并不是 Z[x] 中的元素。
Now that's irreducible because it has degree 1, here would be my c. That looks pretty good, but this isn't good at all: this isn't an element in Z[x].

52
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:58,920
所以问题在于，这些因子可能不在 Z[x] 中。
So the problem is, these factors may not be in Z[x].

53
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:12,439
而事实证明 2x + 1 本身就是 Z[x] 中的一个不可约元、素元；问题在于它不是首一的，你无法在保持它留在 Z[x] 中的同时将它变成首一多项式。
And this itself is an irreducible element, this is a prime element in Z[x], it turns out; and the problem is it's not monic, you can't make it monic and stay in Z[x].

54
00:13:12,439 --> 00:13:26,169
因此我们需要用某种概念来替代“首一多项式”，以便我们能进行某种类似的因式分解，同时确保这些因子确实具有整系数。
So what we need to do is somehow have a replacement of the notion of a monic polynomial that allows us to do some factorization like this, but to ensure that these things actually have integral coefficients.

55
00:13:26,169 --> 00:13:40,000
首一多项式在 Z[x] 中的对应物，就是所谓的本原多项式（primitivepolynomial）。
So the analog of a monic polynomial in Z[x] is what's called a primitive polynomial.

56
00:13:44,199 --> 00:14:08,240
本原多项式（我通常用 f₀ 这类记号表示）具有如下形式：系数全是整数，而“本原”意味着你无法提取任何公因子，它们不全是某个数的倍数。
So a primitive polynomial, I'll call those things like f_0, has the following form: so the coefficients are all integers, and primitive means you can't divide by anything, so they're not all multiples of anything.

57
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:14,360
比如 2x + 1 就是本原多项式，因为它有一个系数是 1，所以你无法从中提取出任何公因子。
Like, this is a primitive polynomial, because it has a coefficient which is 1, so you can't divide anything out of this.

58
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:24,219
本原的意思就是所有系数的最大公因数是 1。
So what primitive means is that the greatest common divisor of all the coefficients is 1.

59
00:14:24,219 --> 00:14:40,992
换句话说，由这些系数生成的理想——在整数环中这是另一种说法——由它们生成的理想是整个整数环 Z。
In other words, that the ideal generated by the coefficients—that's another way of saying it in the integers—the ideal generated by that is all of the integers: the ideal generated by coefficients.

60
00:14:40,992 --> 00:14:47,480
因为如果该理想更小，就意味着存在某个大于 1 的整数整除所有的系数，你可以把它除出来。
Because if the ideal were smaller, that would mean that there was some number that divided all the coefficients and you could divide out.

61
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:54,439
现在大家想一下这个条件，如果把多项式乘上 -1，它仍然满足这个条件。
Now if you think of this condition, you could still preserve that condition if you multiply the polynomial by -1.

62
00:14:54,439 --> 00:15:06,671
负 1。所以如果我把这个多项式写成 -1 · (-2x - 1)，这看起来仍然是一个本原多项式，对吧？
1. So if I took this polynomial and I wrote it as -1 * (-2x - 1), this would still look like a primitive polynomial, right?

63
00:15:06,671 --> 00:15:10,087
因此我甚至不想允许乘上 -1 这种自由度。
So I don't even want to allow myself to do that, to multiply by -1.

64
00:15:10,087 --> 00:15:19,999
所以为了使本原多项式尽可能唯一，我补充的最终条件是：假设非零最高次项系数为正。
So the final condition I do to make my primitive polynomials as unique as possible is I assume that the highest coefficient which is non-zero is actually positive.

65
00:15:19,999 --> 00:15:31,720
有时书上不作此要求，但 Artin 的书里是这么处理的，我认为这是个很好的做法：假设所有系数没有公因数，且最高次项系数为正。
Now sometimes that's not assumed, but the way Artin does it, and I think it's a nice way: you assume that there are no common divisors of the coefficients, and that the highest coefficient is positive.

66
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:51,490
好，那么我断言：整系数多项式环中的任意多项式，都可以唯一地写成一个整数乘上一个本原多项式：f(x) = c · f₀(x)，其中 c 是整数，且该分解唯一。这差不多很显然，对吧？
All right, then I claim that any polynomial over the integers can be written uniquely as an integer times a primitive polynomial: f(x) = c * f_0(x), where c is an integer, and this is unique. Well, that's more or less obvious, isn't it?

67
00:15:51,490 --> 00:16:07,240
我是说，只需算出所有系数的最大公因数并提取出来，作为 c 的初始选择；但问题是剩下的多项式最高次项系数可能不为正，如果不为正，就把 c 乘上 -1。
I mean, I just see what the greatest common divisor is, I pull that out, that's going to be my initial choice for c; but then the problem is that this thing might not have a positive coefficient, so if it doesn't have a positive coefficient, I multiply that c by -1.

68
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:23,720
这就是我的 c，剩下的就是一个本原多项式，之后就无法再做任何提取了：因为它的系数 gcd 为 1，而且我也不能乘上任何整数，否则要么会制造出公因数，要么会改变首项系数的符号。
So that's my c, and then I'm left with a primitive polynomial, and then there's nothing more I can do: I can't pull out anything of this because it has gcd 1, and I can't multiply it by any integer because that would either create a gcd or it would change the sign of the first coefficient.

69
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,647
2x + 1 本身就是本原的。
So this is already primitive.

70
00:16:25,647 --> 00:16:44,840
但如果我有一个多项式如 6x² - 3x + 9，那就会写成 3· (2x² - x + 3)，这里的 3 就是 c，而 2x² - x + 3 就是 f₀，因为所有这些系数都可以被 3 整除。
But if I had a polynomial like 6x^2 - 3x + 9, then that would be written as 3 times (2x^2 - x + 3), and this would be the c and this would be the f_0, because all these coefficients were divisible by 3.

71
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:58,959
好，关于这一点最妙的是，不仅整系数多项式有这样的表达式，对于有理系数多项式也有！
Okay, now what's cool about this, what's particularly cool about it, is that not only do I have such an expression for an integer polynomial, I have it for a rational polynomial!

72
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:35,194
这非常有趣：事实上，若 f(x) 具有有理系数，你也可以将 f(x) 写成 c · f₀(x)，其中 f₀(x) 是 Z[x] 中的本原多项式，而 c 是一个有理数，并且该表达式是唯一的。
And that's very interesting: in fact, if f(x) has rational coefficients, then you can write f(x) as c * f_0(x), where this is primitive in Z[x] and this is a rational number, and this expression is unique.

73
00:17:35,194 --> 00:17:44,040
因此任何有理多项式都唯一确定一个本原整系数多项式和一个有理数，就像任何整多项式都确定一个整数和一个本原多项式一样。
So that any rational polynomial determines a primitive integral polynomial and a rational number, just like any integer polynomial determines an integer and a primitive polynomial.

74
00:17:44,040 --> 00:18:07,256
我们来看看这是怎么运作的：从有理多项式出发，它只有有限多个系数；每个系数的分母只有有限多个因子，因此存在一个整数——我可以用一个足够大的整数 N 去乘 f(x)，
So let's see how that works: I just start with my rational polynomial, that has only finitely many coefficients; each coefficient has only finitely many denominators in it, so there's an integer—I can multiply f(x) by a large integer N,

75
00:18:07,256 --> 00:18:37,080
使得 N 乘它的所有系数对所有 i 都是整数，即 N · f(x) ∈ Z[x]。对吧？然后我将其唯一地写成 d · f₀(x)，其中 d 是整数，f₀ 是本原多项式。
so that N times its coefficients are integers for all i, so N * f(x) is in Z[x]. Okay? And then I write that uniquely as a d * f_0(x), where d is an integer and f_0 is a primitive polynomial.

76
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:44,920
这样我就得到了 f(x) = (d/N) · f₀(x)。
And then I've got an f(x) written as (d/N) * f_0(x).

77
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:53,880
于是它被写成了一个有理数乘上一个本原多项式。好，然后你唯一需要做的就是验证这种表示是唯一的。
So it's written as a rational number times a primitive polynomial. Okay, and then the only thing you have to do is check that this is unique.

78
00:18:53,880 --> 00:19:10,640
其唯一性基本上很显然，大家可以看一下书中关于该分解唯一性的简要证明，但是，我是说，我们这里得到的 f₀ 是唯一的这一点基本很清楚，因为如果我们乘上一个更大的 N，我们也只是从系数中把那个倍数提取出来。
It's more or less obvious it's unique, I'll let you take a look at the brief proof in the book that it's unique decomposition, but, uh, I mean, it's more or less clear that what we get here, f_0, is unique, because if we multiply by a bigger N, we would just pull that amount out of f_0.

79
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:26,800
好，关于这个分解非常妙且至关重要的一点（我们稍后会看到）是：你可以从这个分解中判断多项式何时是整系数的、何时不是，这是唯一性的一部分：事实上，
Okay, now what's cool about this, and this is very important as we're going to see, is that you can tell from this decomposition when your polynomial is integral and when it isn't, and that's part of uniqueness:

80
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:46,368
f(x) ∈ Z[x]当且仅当这个常数属于 Z。顺便说一下，这个常数被称为“容量”（content，又称内容），这是高斯的术语；我们只是在重温高斯关于多项式的一些工作。
in fact, f(x) is in Z[x] if and only if this constant is in Z. This constant, by the way, is called the content—that's an expression of Gauss's; we're just redoing some of Gauss's work on polynomials.

81
00:19:46,368 --> 00:19:56,320
取任意有理多项式，将其写成一个有理数乘上一个本原多项式，然后你会发现该多项式是整系数的，当且仅当该常数是整数。
So you take any rational polynomial, you write it as a rational number times a primitive polynomial, and then you find that the polynomial is integral if and only if that constant is an integer.

82
00:19:56,320 --> 00:20:06,670
我们来看看为什么：如果多项式是整系数的，那么显然该常数是整数，你只需提取出所有系数的最大公因数即可，这部分很简单。
Well, let's see why: if the polynomial is integral, then it's clear the constant is an integer, you just divide out by the greatest common divisor of all the coefficients, so that part is easy.

83
00:20:06,670 --> 00:20:17,800
另一方面，若容量是整数，那么 c · f₀(x) 显然就是整系数多项式。
Now on the other hand, if the content is an integer, then this expression c * f_0(x) is an integer polynomial.

84
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:39,425
好，所以我们就证完了。好。现在，这就是我要如何在 Z 中进行分解的方法，非常漂亮：我取在有理数域上的分解，并把所有这些首一不可约多项式替换为它们的本原部分。
Okay, so we just did it. Okay. Okay, now here's how I'm going to do this factorization in Z, very cool: I take this factorization in the rational numbers, and I replace all these irreducible monic polynomials by their primitive parts.

85
00:20:39,425 --> 00:21:01,479
我把它写成 c · c₁ q₁(x) ...q₁(x) · c₂ q₂(x) ··· c_k q_k(x)。
So I write this as c * c_1 q_1(x) ... let's call it q_1(x) * c_2 q_2(x) ... * c_k q_k(x).

86
00:21:01,479 --> 00:21:26,311
我把它重写为 d（即 c 与所有 c₁ 到 c_k 的乘积）乘上 q₁(x) ... q_k(x)，其中这些现在都是在 Q[x] 中不可约的本原多项式，因为它们只是那些首一不可约多项式的标量倍。
So I rewrite that as d, which is the product of c and all the c_1 through c_k, times q_1(x) ... q_k(x), where these are now primitive polynomials which are irreducible in Q[x], because they're just scalar multiples of these irreducible monic polynomials.

87
00:21:26,311 --> 00:21:43,701
因此每个首一多项式我都写成一个常数乘上一个本原多项式，就像我刚才举的例子：那个 2x + 1 我写成 2 · (x + 1/2)，若从x + 1/2 出发，就会写成 1/2 · (2x + 1)。
So each monic polynomial I write as a constant times a primitive polynomial, just like I did for that example: this 2x + 1 which I'd written as 2 * (x + 1/2), I would have started by this x + 1/2 and written it as 1/2 * (2x + 1).

88
00:21:43,701 --> 00:21:49,320
这就是典型的转化：如果 p₁ 是 x +1/2，我会把它写成 1/2 · (2x + 1)。
So this would be a typical conversion: if p_1 were x plus a half, I'd write it as 1/2 * (2x + 1).

89
00:21:49,320 --> 00:22:09,520
所以我把这些有理数 c₁, c₂, ..., c_k 提出来，全部并入常数 d（即 c · c₁ · c₂ ··· c_k），然后就留下了若干本原整系数多项式，它们本身在 Q[x] 中是不可约的。
So I pull out these rational numbers c_1, c_2, ..., c_k, I pull them all into the constant d, which is c * c_1 * c_2 ... * c_k, and then I'm left with primitive integral polynomials, which themselves are irreducible in Q[x].

90
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:28,760
事实上，好，我断言：当我把多项式写成这种形式时，该多项式具有整系数当且仅当这个常数 d 是一个整数。
In fact, okay, I claim that when I write the polynomial this way, that the polynomial has integral coefficients if and only if this constant is an integer.

91
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:40,240
好，如果常数是整数，后面的多项式乘积具有整系数，所以如果用一个整数去乘整系数多项式，就会得到整系数多项式。好，这就是这个方向。
Okay, if the constant is an integer, this has got integer coefficients, so if you multiply a polynomial of integer coefficients by an integer, you get an integral polynomial. Okay, so that's this direction.

92
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:53,280
若多项式具有整系数，对吧，那么我们看到它可以通过提取系数的最大公因数写成一个整数乘上一个本原多项式。
If the polynomial has integral coefficients, right, then we saw that it could be written as an integer times a primitive polynomial by taking this integer which is the greatest common divisor of its coefficients.

93
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:59,987
由于这种表示是唯一的，这就说明如果你从整系数多项式出发，它的容量必然是整数。
Since this expression is unique, that shows that if you start with something of integral coefficients, you get an integral content.

94
00:22:59,987 --> 00:23:09,840
这就是为什么你可以仅仅通过考察因式分解中的容量，就能判断该多项式是否具有整系数。
So that's why you can tell whether your polynomial has integral coefficients just by looking at its content in this factorization.

95
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:17,699
不，我刚才没说它一定是整数，你说得很对，它属于 Q。
No, I didn't say it was an integer, you're absolutely right, it's in Q.

96
00:23:17,699 --> 00:23:24,050
不不，完全正确：首先，d 原本可能在 Q 中；其次，所有这些因子最初都在 Q 中。
No, no, absolutely right: first of all, this could have been in Q; secondly, all of these could have been in Q.

97
00:23:24,050 --> 00:23:39,280
所以到目前为止，我们只说明了任何整多项式都可以写成一个有理数乘上一组在 Q[x] 中不可约的本原多项式的乘积。我们快推导到了，但还没完成！
So so far what we've got is we've shown that any integral polynomial can be written as a rational number times a product of primitive polynomials which are irreducible with rational coefficients. We're getting there, we're not there yet!

98
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:51,919
顺便说一下，我要向大家证明这个 d 确实是整数，但我还没证出来，目前我们只走到这一步。提得好。好，现在请看高斯著名的引理！
And by the way, I'm going to show you that this is an integer, but I haven't done it yet, so far we're just here. Good point. Okay, now here's Gauss's great lemma!

99
00:23:54,120 --> 00:24:23,079
高斯有许多著名的引理：在二次互反律的证明中还有另一个高斯引理，但这是他关于多项式的引理：若 f₀ 与 g₀ 是本原多项式，则它们的乘积 f₀ · g₀ 也是本原多项式。
Gauss has a lot of very famous lemmas: there's another Gauss's lemma that goes into the proof of quadratic reciprocity, but here's his lemma on polynomials: If f_0 and g_0 are primitive polynomials, so is their product f_0 * g_0.

100
00:24:23,079 --> 00:24:33,000
特别地，这个乘积将是一个本原多项式，因为它是本原多项式的乘积。
So in particular, this product is going to be a primitive polynomial, because it's the product of primitive polynomials.

101
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:55,959
现在，为了不让大家悬着，我来证明这个 d 为什么是整数：因为我已经把 f(x) 写成了一个有理数乘上一个本原多项式，但这种表示是唯一的，而 f(x) 又是整系数多项式，因此它必须是整数！
Now, because I don't want to leave you hanging, I'll show you that this is an integer: because I've written f(x) as a rational number times a primitive polynomial, but that expression is unique, and f(x) is an integral polynomial, therefore this has to be an integer!

102
00:24:55,959 --> 00:25:03,079
很精彩吧？但大家明白，仅知道其中每一个都是本原的还不够，我必须以某种方式知道它们的乘积也是本原的。
Brilliant, huh? But you see, just knowing that each one of these is primitive is not enough; I have to somehow know that their product is primitive.

103
00:25:03,079 --> 00:25:27,240
这就是高斯引理。大家看这个证明是多么绝妙：若不然，设素数 p 整除f₀(x) · g₀(x) 的所有系数。
So that's Gauss's lemma. Now watch how this goes, this is an absolutely wonderful proof: if not, say the prime p divides all the coefficients of f_0(x) * g_0(x).

104
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:55,158
这就是多项式非本原时的情况：系数的 gcd 不为1，因而有某个素数整除 gcd，即某个素数整除所有系数。好。现在考虑环同态，将整系数多项式映为系数模 p 的多项式：
That's what happens when you don't have a primitive polynomial: the gcd is not 1, so some prime divides the gcd, so some prime divides all the coefficients. Okay. Now consider the homomorphism, the ring homomorphism that takes polynomials with integer coefficients to polynomials

105
00:25:55,158 --> 00:26:25,039
它把整数 a 映为 a mod p，并把 x 映为 x，所以它只是把系数模 p 约化。它把多项式 ∑ a_n x^n映为 ∑ ā_n x^n，其中这是模 p 的系数。
with coefficients mod p, that takes a polynomial—well, it takes an integer a -> a mod p, and it takes x to x, so it just reduces the coefficients mod p. It takes a polynomial sum a_n x^n to sum a_n-bar x^n, where this is the coefficient mod p.

106
00:26:25,039 --> 00:26:33,679
这是一个同态，因为我已经说明了它在整数上的作用，以及它在生成元 x 上的作用，然后通过乘法自然延拓。
That's a homomorphism because I told you what it does on the integers, and I told you what it does on the generator, and then you just extend multiplicatively.

107
00:26:33,679 --> 00:27:09,400
如果素数 p 整除它的所有系数，那就说明这个多项式在该同态下的像是 0，好，这意味着（因为这是环同态）f̄₀ 与 ḡ₀ 的乘积为 0，因为乘积的像等于像的乘积。
That says if a prime divides all the coefficients of this, that says that the image of this polynomial under this homomorphism is 0, okay, which means, because this is a ring homomorphism, that the product of f_0-bar and g_0-bar is 0, because the image of the product is the product of the images.

108
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:13,520
好，这有什么问题？
Okay, now what's wrong with that?

109
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:29,600
为什么？因为这个环是域上的多项式环！请记住，Z/pZ 是一个域，所以 (Z/pZ)[x] 是一个整环！
Why? Because this ring is polynomials over a field! Remember, Z/pZ is a field, so (Z/pZ)[x] is an integral domain!

110
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:51,320
而这里两个元素的乘积等于 0，这就意味着要么 f̄₀ = 0，要么 ḡ₀= 0，但这与这些多项式是本原多项式的事实矛盾，即没有任何素数能整除它们的所有系数。
And here we have the product of two elements is 0, so that implies that either f_0-bar = 0 or g_0-bar = 0, and that contradicts the fact that these polynomials are primitive, so that no prime divides all their coefficients.

111
00:27:51,320 --> 00:27:53,658
所以这是高斯的一个极其出色的论证。
So this is a really great argument of Gauss.

112
00:27:53,658 --> 00:28:03,100
当然在那个时代还没有环和同态这些现代概念，他必须从零开始推导。好，这就是高斯引理。
Of course it was before there were rings and homomorphisms or anything like that, so he had to do it from complete scratch. Okay, so that's Gauss's lemma.

113
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:16,960
它告诉我们，到这里我们几乎大功告成了：它告诉我们现在我们得到了一个分解式，其中由于乘积是本原的，常数 d 确实是一个整数。
And that tells us we're almost done here: that tells us that now we have a factorization where, since this product is primitive, this constant is actually an integer.

114
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:35,787
现在我要展示高斯发现的另一件很酷的事情：这些多项式——既然它们在 Q[x] 中不可约，那么它们在 Z[x] 中也必然不可约，对吧？我是说，如果能在整数环中分解，当然就能在有理数域中分解，对吧？
And now I'm going to show you another cool thing that Gauss discovered, which is that these polynomials— well, if they're irreducible in Q[x], they're also irreducible in Z[x], right? I mean, if I could factor them in the integers, I could have certainly factored them in the rational numbers, right?

115
00:28:35,787 --> 00:28:43,624
所以这些多项式在整数环中无法进一步分解，它们是 Z[x] 中的素元。
So that these things cannot be factored any further in the integers, so they're prime elements of Z[x].

116
00:28:43,624 --> 00:28:49,869
因此为了获得素元分解，我只需进一步把这个整数 d 分解为普通的素数。
So to obtain a prime factorization, all I have to do is further factor this integer, which I do into normal primes.

117
00:28:49,869 --> 00:29:17,593
我现在把它写成 ± p₁ p₂ ...这些是普通的整数素数 p_l · q₁(x) ... q_k(x)，其中这些整数素数在 Z[x] 中当然也是素元，并且这些是 Z[x] 中的本原不可约多项式。
So I write that now as plus or minus p_1 p_2 ... these are normal integer primes, p_l * q_1(x) ... q_k(x), where these are integer primes which are certainly prime in Z[x], and these are primitive irreducible polynomials in Z[x].

118
00:29:17,593 --> 00:29:27,079
这就是任意整多项式在 Z[x] 中分解为素元的分解式。
And this is a decomposition of an arbitrary polynomial into prime elements in Z[x].

119
00:29:27,079 --> 00:29:35,320
再稍加努力（不会太多，我在此不展开讲，大家可以看书），就能证明这种分解是唯一的。
And a little more work, not too much, which I'm not going to do here but you can read in the book, will show you that this decomposition is unique.

120
00:29:35,320 --> 00:29:59,117
这就是因式分解定理：任何整系数多项式，首先确定整除其容量的一组素数，即其容量的素因子分解；然后它确定一组不可约本原多项式，
And that's the factorization: any integer polynomial determines, first, a set of primes which divide its content, which is the prime factorization of the prime factorization of the content of f(x); and then it determines a bunch of irreducible

121
00:29:59,117 --> 00:30:17,186
它们在某种意义上一一对应于其在有理数域上因式分解中的首一因子，你只是去掉了它们的分母并使它们变为本原多项式；它们具有相同的次数等等。
primitive polynomials, which in some sense correspond in a one-to-one way to the monic factors of its factorization in the rational numbers, and you've just sort of cleared out their denominators and made them primitive; they have the same degrees, etc.

122
00:30:17,186 --> 00:30:28,805
因此这里的因式分解与在有理数域上的分解非常相似，除了你提取出了整数容量，这就是整个定理的完成。现在大家可能会问：那何必去关心 Z[x] 中的因式分解呢？
So the factorization looks very similar to what it does in the rational numbers, except you pull out you pull out this integer content, and that's the completion of it. Now you may say, well, why worry about factorization in Z[x] at all?

123
00:30:28,805 --> 00:30:45,600
原因在于：证明 Z[x] 中的多项式不可约，比在 Q[x] 中证明容易得多！
And the reason: it's easier to prove polynomials in Z[x] are irreducible than in Q[x]!

124
00:30:45,600 --> 00:30:52,159
而且事实证明还有一条结论：一个本原多项式在 Z[x] 中不可约当且仅当它在 Q[x] 中不可约。
And it turns out there's another thing, that a polynomial is irreducible in Z[x] if and only if it's irreducible in Q[x].

125
00:30:52,159 --> 00:30:59,919
而之所以更容易证明多项式不可约，是因为我们能利用这个同态！
And the reason it's easier to prove that polynomials are irreducible is because we have the benefit of this homomorphism!

126
00:30:59,919 --> 00:31:14,277
大家看，如果有这样一个同态，而你想检验这里面的某个元素是否不可约，你可以考察它在目标环中的像。如果你在目标环中无法分解它的像，那么你在原环中当然也无法分解它！
You see, if you have a homomorphism like this, and you want to test: is something in here irreducible, you can take its image in here. If you can't factor the image in here, you certainly couldn't have factored it in here!

127
00:31:14,277 --> 00:31:26,040
我是说，如果你在原环中有某个多项式想研究，并且它能分解为 m · n，那么当你取 f-bar 时，它就等于 m̄(x) · n̄(x)。
I mean, if you have some polynomial here that you want to study and you have it factored as m * n, then when you take f-bar, that's m-bar(x) * n-bar(x).

128
00:31:26,040 --> 00:31:33,959
假设你选取的素数不整除最高次项系数，那么它们的次数与 m 和 n 相同。
These have the same degree as m and n, assuming you've chosen a prime where the highest coefficient isn't divisible by p.

129
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:43,400
并且如果在这个商环中没有任何因式分解，那么你在原环中就不可能存在因式分解，因此在原环中它必然不可约。
And so if you didn't have any factorization in this ring, then you couldn't have had a factorization here, and it would have been irreducible here.

130
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:49,560
而在有限域多项式环中，检验不可约性非常容易，因为每个次数的多项式只有有限多个！
And here it's easy to check whether things are irreducible, because you only have finitely many polynomials of each degree to try!

131
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:58,227
所以如果我有一个二元域上 4 次的多项式，我只需要看它是否能被 1 次、2 次或 3 次的多项式整除。
So if I have a polynomial of degree 4 with coefficients in the field of 2 elements, I only have to see whether it's divisible by things of degree 1, 2, and 3.

132
00:31:58,227 --> 00:32:05,563
而我可以列出二元域上所有 1 次、2 次和 3 次的多项式，因为系数只有 0或 1！
And I can list the polynomials of degree 1, 2, and 3 over the field of 2 elements, because the coefficients are just 0 or 1!

133
00:32:05,563 --> 00:32:11,605
而在整数环中我无法列出所有 4 次以内的多项式，更不用说在有理数域中了。
Whereas I can't list the polynomials up to degree 4 in here, let alone in the rational numbers.

134
00:32:11,605 --> 00:32:26,680
所以对于一个 4 次多项式，我在有理数域上可能很难做因式分解，但如果我把它乘上一个整数化为整多项式，然后模一个素数进行约化，并发现它在那里是不可约的，那么它在原环中也就是不可约的！
So a polynomial of degree 4, I might have trouble factoring over the rational numbers, but if I multiply it by an integer, get it to the integers, and then I reduce it modulo a prime and I discover that it's irreducible there, then it was irreducible back here!

135
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:46,280
所以证明多项式在 Z[x] 中不可约更容易，因为你可以在某个像中检验其不可约性；而你不能把 Q[x] 映到这里，因为p 在 Q[x] 中不是素元，但你可以把 Z[x] 映过去。
So it's easier to prove polynomials are irreducible in Z[x], as you can check irreducibility in some image; and you can't map Q[x] to this because p is not a prime in Q[x], but you can map Z[x] to it.

136
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:57,840
我来给大家举一个例子。
So I'll give you one example of that.

137
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:10,737
例题——书中还给出了很多其他例子，让我看看能不能找个好例子。
Example—and the book does many others, let's see if I can find a good one.

138
00:33:10,737 --> 00:33:36,951
噢，手头好像没有现成的好例子……噢，我们来看 x³ + x + 1 吧。这是 f(x)，它是不可约的。证明：考察它在(Z/2Z)[x] 中的像。
Oh, I don't seem to have a good example... Oh, I don't know, let's take, uh, x^3 + x + 1. That's f(x), is irreducible. Proof: look at the image in (Z/2Z)[x].

139
00:33:37,319 --> 00:33:48,633
它能分解为 f(x) = m(x) · n(x) 吗？这是 3 次多项式。
Does it factor: f(x) = m(x) * n(x)? Well, this is of degree 3.

140
00:33:48,633 --> 00:33:55,959
如果它有非平凡分解，其中一个必为 1 次，另一个必为 2 次。
If I had a non-trivial factorization, one of these things would have degree 1, one would have degree 2.

141
00:33:55,959 --> 00:34:14,040
好，因为它们的次数相加必须等于 3，所以如果它在 (Z/2Z)[x] 中可约，其中一个必然是 1 次的，即形如 x + a，另一个是 x² + bx + c。
Okay, I mean, they have to add up to degree 3, so if it factored in (Z/2Z)[x], one of these would be of degree 1, so it would look like x + a, and then it would be x^2 + bx + c.

142
00:34:14,040 --> 00:34:36,480
好，这就意味着该多项式在二元域中有一个根，从而在 Z/2Z 中 f(-a) = 0。所以如果有分解，就必须有根；但很容易验证这个多项式在二元域上没有根，因为二元域中只有两个元素：0 和 1。
Okay, which means that I have a root of the polynomial in the field of 2 elements, so then f(-a) = 0 in Z/2Z. So if you had a factorization, you would have a root; but it's easy to check that this polynomial has no roots over the field of 2 elements, because there are only two things in the field of 2 elements: 0 and 1.

143
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:48,679
如果代入 0，f(0) = 1；如果代入 1，f(1) = 1 + 1 + 1 = 1。所以这不可能发生，因此不存在因式分解。
If you put in 0, f(0) = 1; and if you put in 1, f(1) = 1 + 1 + 1 = 1. So this doesn't happen, therefore there's no factorization.

144
00:34:48,679 --> 00:34:56,089
现在大家可能会说：那 4 次多项式呢？是啊，4 次多项式怎么办？
Now you might say, well, what about a polynomial of degree 4? Yeah, what about a polynomial of degree 4?

145
00:34:56,089 --> 00:35:13,778
不知道，我们来试一个 4 次多项式，看看我能不能搞定它，嗯：我可以试试这个：x⁴ + x³ + 1。希望它是不可约的。我们可以看它在模 2 整数环的多项式环 (Z/2Z)[x] 中的像。
I don't know, let's try a polynomial of degree 4 and see if I can hack it, um: I could try this: x^4 + x^3 + 1. Let's hope that that's irreducible. Well, we could look at the image in Z mod 2 of x, (Z/2Z)[x].

146
00:35:13,778 --> 00:35:22,280
它显然不能分解为一个 1 次乘 3 次，因为同样它没有根：0 和 1 都不是根。
It certainly doesn't factor as a degree 1 times a degree 3, because again it has no roots: 0 and 1 are not roots.

147
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:30,280
另一方面，也许它可以分解为 2 次乘 2 次？
On the other hand, maybe it factors as a degree 2 times a degree 2?

148
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:36,600
好，同样，这两个 2 次因子必须是不可约的，因为它没有根。
Okay, so again these degree 2 factors have to be irreducible, because we have no roots.

149
00:35:36,600 --> 00:35:43,800
所以我只需要看二元域上有哪些可能的 2 次不可约多项式，而其实只有一个！
So I just have to look at what are the possible irreducible polynomials of degree 2 over the field of 2 elements, and there's only one of them!

150
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:52,600
二元域上唯一的 2 次不可约多项式就是 x² + x + 1，因为你必须写出一个没有任何根的多项式。
The only irreducible polynomial of degree 2 over the field of 2 elements is this, because you have to write down something without any roots.

151
00:35:52,600 --> 00:35:57,839
所以唯一的问题是：这个多项式能整除原多项式吗？
So the only question is: does this polynomial divide this polynomial?

152
00:35:57,839 --> 00:36:03,960
答案是否定的，因为唯一的可能性是，如果它能整除，商式也必然是另一个 2 次多项式。
The answer is no, because the only possibility, if it divided it, you'd be left with something else of degree 2.

153
00:36:03,960 --> 00:36:08,679
所以唯一的可能性就是它必须是这个多项式的平方，对吧？
So the only possibility is you'd have to square this polynomial, right?

154
00:36:08,679 --> 00:36:16,680
但这个多项式的平方不等于原多项式：该多项式的平方事实上是 (x² + x + 1)² = x⁴ + x² + 1。
But the square of this polynomial is not equal to that polynomial: the square of this polynomial is in fact x to the fourth plus x squared plus one.

155
00:36:16,680 --> 00:36:22,320
所以它不等于 x⁴ + x³ + 1，因此它在 Z[x] 中是不可约的。
So it's not equal to this, so this is irreducible in Z[x].

156
00:36:24,639 --> 00:36:27,839
请提问。
Please?

157
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:43,142
因为任何其他 2 次多项式都会有线性因子。Atticus，我们来看一下所有的 2 次多项式，你就明白我的意思了。这是2 次不可约的。
Because any other polynomial of degree 2 would have a linear factor. Let's look at the polynomials of degree 2, Atticus, so you see what I mean. This is irreducible of degree 2.

158
00:36:43,142 --> 00:37:04,560
其他 2 次多项式形如 x² + 1 和 x² + x（只有这两个），或者就是 x²：这就是二元域上所有的 4 个 2 次多项式，因为最高次项系数必须为 1，所以这里的系数有 0 或 1 两种选择，常数项也有 0 或 1 两种选择。
The other polynomials of degree 2 would look like x^2 + 1 and x^2 + x, those are the only two, or just x^2: those are—those are the 4 polynomials of degree 2, because it has to start off with the coefficient 1, so you have a choice of 0 or 1 here, or 0 or 1 here, that's it.

159
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:14,680
x² 和 x² + x 显然有根 x = 0，而 x² + 1 显然有根x = 1，这些都有根，所以它们不是不可约的！
This clearly has a root x = 0, this clearly has a root x = 1, and this has roots x = 0 and x = 1. So they're not irreducible!

160
00:37:14,680 --> 00:37:23,839
所以如果能分解——我们已经确认过它没有线性因子，那么如果它拆成两个 2 次式，它们两个都必须是2 次不可约多项式。
So if I factor—we already agreed it had no linear factors, so if it split 2 and 2, these would both have to be irreducible of degree 2.

161
00:37:25,639 --> 00:37:31,960
因为如果它们可约，就会有 1 次因子，而我们已经确认过该多项式没有任何1 次因子。
Because if they had a factor, it would have a factor of degree 1, and we agreed this polynomial had no factors of degree 1.

162
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:44,400
大家掌握要领了吧？所以这个方法变得极其有用：转化为整多项式、提取容量等等。如果你想要研究在有理数域中的因式分解，
You get the hang of this? So it becomes extremely useful to use this: moving to the integer polynomial and the content and everything, if you want to study factorization even in the rational numbers,

163
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:52,280
你可以在整数环中检验；而要在整数环中检验因式分解，你只需模一个充分恰当选取的素数 p 检验因式分解。
you test factorization in the integers; and to test factorization over the integers, you check factorization modulo a sufficiently well-chosen prime p.

164
00:37:52,280 --> 00:38:04,919
现在我必须提醒大家一件非常有趣的事：可能存在某些在整数环上不可约的多项式，但模每个素数 p都会分解！
Now I have to warn you about something that's very amusing: there can be polynomials which are irreducible over the integers, but for every prime p they factor!

165
00:38:04,919 --> 00:38:25,720
Artin 的书中给出了这样的例子，这有点让人头疼。请问？如果你分解的不是首一多项式，你只需要避开整除最高次项系数的素数即可，仅此而已，而几乎所有素数都满足条件。
Artin gives an example of that, that was slightly annoying. Yes? If you're not factoring a monic polynomial, you have to stay away from primes that divide the leading coefficient, that's all, and that's almost all primes.

166
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:37,359
你们看，这个论证（即约化多项式得到分解时因子具有相同的次数）是基于最高次项系数不被 p 整除的事实。
See, this argument that when you reduce a polynomial and you get a factorization, the factors have the same degree, is based on the fact that the leading coefficient of this polynomial is not divisible by p.

167
00:38:37,359 --> 00:38:49,480
因此对于任何给定的整系数多项式，其首项系数只被有限多个素数 p 整除：把它们扔掉，用其余的素数来检验不可约性。
So any given polynomial that you're studying with coefficients in the integers, the leading coefficient is only divisible by a finite number of primes p: throw them away, and use the other primes to test irreducibility.

168
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:55,680
好，很好的问题，因为我们遇到的不一定是首一多项式。
Okay, good question, because we don't necessarily have monic polynomials.

169
00:38:55,680 --> 00:39:04,700
Peter 和我给大家布置了若干道因式分解的习题；这是理论中非常重要的部分，在实际计算中非常实用。
So Peter and I have assigned a number of factoring exercises for you; this is an important part of the theory, and it's very useful in practical computations.

170
00:39:04,700 --> 00:39:11,086
例如它在编码理论中极其有用：你们当中以后从事编码理论研究的同学会学到，构造二元域上具有高次数且不可约的多项式非常有用。
It's extremely useful in coding theory, for example: those of you who go on and work in coding theory will learn it's very useful

171
00:39:11,086 --> 00:39:21,240
一个至今尚未被证明的重要猜想是——首先，已知在二元域上任意次数都存在不可约多项式，这并不显然，对吧？
to construct polynomials, say over the field of 2 elements, that are irreducible and have large degree.

172
00:39:26,665 --> 00:39:38,720
我们刚才在二次多项式中只是运气好，恰好只有一个不可约的；但从域论中我们知道任意次数都存在不可约多项式 f(x)。
I mean, we just got lucky in quadratic polynomials, there was just one that was irreducible; but it's known from the theory of fields there's an irreducible f(x) of any degree.

173
00:39:38,720 --> 00:39:58,546
在编码理论中非常有用的结论是：证明你总能构造一个形如这样的 f(x)：三项式，即除首尾外只有另一个非零项。在二元域上每个次数都存在不可约三项式吗？
What would be very useful in coding theory is to prove that you could always make an f(x) that looked like this: a trinomial, namely with only two other coefficients. Is there an irreducible trinomial of every degree over the field of 2 elements?

174
00:39:58,546 --> 00:40:07,529
人们已经用计算机验证了，我不知道，可能验证到了10,000 次甚至 100,000 次，我不知道目前的计算纪录是多少；但没人能证明总存在不可约三项式。
People have checked it, I don't know, up to degree 10,000, maybe 100,000, I don't know what the current computational record is; no one can prove there's always an irreducible trinomial.

175
00:40:07,529 --> 00:40:20,600
从编码理论和序列计算的角度来看，这会让计算方便得多。实际上它会长成这样，因为二元域中的非零系数只有 1。
From the point of view of coding theory and making computations of sequences, this would make life a lot easier. Actually it would look like this, because the non-zero coefficients in the field of 2 elements are just 0 and 1.

176
00:40:20,600 --> 00:40:23,472
所以这只是一门美妙理论的开端。
So this is just the beginning of a fabulous theory.

177
00:40:23,472 --> 00:40:36,662
但我想在下节课多讲一些高斯整数环的内容，以及二次域中的整数环，所以我今天讲多项式就到此为止。这并不意味着你们应该停止学习多项式，但我今天就讲到这里。在这门课之后。
But I want to do a little bit more on the Gaussian integers and about integers in quadratic fields, so I'm going to stop with polynomials here. That doesn't mean you should stop with polynomials here, but I'm going to stop in this course.

178
00:40:36,662 --> 00:40:44,430
当大家修读 Math 123 时，你们将系统学习伽罗瓦理论；而伽罗瓦理论本质上就是研究整系数一元多项式，仅此而已！
When you take Math 123, you're going to learn all about Galois theory; and Galois theory is just the study of polynomials in one variable with coefficients in the integers, that's it!

179
00:40:44,430 --> 00:40:46,800
这样概括很贴切。
That's a good way of saying it.

180
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:52,921
现在我想请大家做的是，如果可以的话，用剩下的课堂时间填写 CUE 课程评估表。
But what I'm going to ask you to do now, if you can, is to take the rest of the class to fill out the CUE guide.

181
00:40:52,921 --> 00:41:02,400
我作为系主任，会根据教授们在 CUE 评估表上的低分严肃惩戒他们，所以我可不想让大家逼得我惩戒自己，那可太糟糕了！
So I discipline professors vigilantly on the basis of their low scores on the CUE guide, so I don't want you to have me discipline myself, that would be very bad!

182
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:12,280
请大家把评估表分发下去，在分发的同时我作个简短说明。大家需要填写：谁是教授 A、谁是习题课助教 A等等。
I'll ask you to pass them out, and while you pass them out I'm going to make a little announcement. So you're supposed to fill out: you know, who's Professor A, who's Section Leader A, etc.

183
00:41:12,280 --> 00:41:24,760
在这份表格上我是教授 A。请尽量使用铅笔，如果没有就用黑笔，不要使用红墨水。
So I am Professor A on this form. You should use a pencil if possible, if not, a black pen; do not use red ink.

184
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:44,360
那么，教授 A 正是我，而你们的习题课导师是 Peter Kronheimer，填在背面。我们不对助教打分，尽管他们做得非常出色。
So, Professor A happens to be me, and your section leader happens to be Peter Kronheimer, that's on the back. We don't evaluate the TAs even though they've done a fabulous job.

185
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:48,000
所以请大家用剩下的时间认真填写。
So please take the rest of class, take your time.

186
00:41:48,000 --> 00:42:03,116
我非常看重这些反馈，如果到时我还没被折腾疯的话，我明年大概还会教这门课，我很希望了解大家对授课内容、进度、难易适宜度，以及是否有所收获的意见。
I really do use these things enormously, I'm going to probably teach this next year if I maintain my sanity until that point, and I would like to get your comments on the material covered, the speed, the appropriateness of it, whether you got anything out of this.

187
00:42:03,116 --> 00:42:06,240
我承受得住批评，真的，相信我，这对我很有帮助！
I can take it, I can take it, believe me, it would help me!

188
00:42:06,240 --> 00:42:14,602
另外我还需要一位志愿者，在下课后把表格收齐并送回大学大楼（University Hall），因为按规定我和 Peter 都不能再碰这些表格了。
And I also need a volunteer who at the end of the class will collect these and take them back to University Hall, because I'm not supposed to touch them anymore, and neither is Peter.

189
00:42:14,602 --> 00:42:22,000
有谁今天晚些时候顺路去大学大楼并愿意帮忙收一下吗？好的，多谢，多谢！
Does anyone have a chance to go back to University Hall later today and can collect them? And thanks, thanks!

190
00:42:23,240 --> 00:42:30,162
送到大学大楼一楼。
First floor of University Hall.
